 &lt;span
 
 class="dark:text-neutral-300"
 
 &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update 2026:&lt;/strong&gt; I no longer use mTLS. The technology is great, but it turned me into IT support for my family. My public services now sit behind CrowdSec and passkeys. See &lt;a href="https://dominikbritz.com/posts/my-ai-managed-home-server-in-2026/#a-public-edge-without-client-certificates" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;My AI-Managed Home Server in 2026&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This article explains how to securely access your home server and its services with mTLS and WireGuard.&lt;/p&gt;</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://dominikbritz.com/posts/secure-remote-access/featured.jpg"/></item><item><title>Immich: Self-Hosted Photo Gallery With Cloud Backup &amp; OpenID Connect</title><link>https://dominikbritz.com/posts/immich-self-hosted-photos-with-cloud-backup/</link><pubDate>Sun, 24 Mar 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dominikbritz.com/posts/immich-self-hosted-photos-with-cloud-backup/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This article explains how to set up a self-hosted photo gallery with Immich including cloud backup and OpenID Connect to Authelia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is part of my series on creating a home server on an old laptop. I’m assuming that you’ve set up Docker, Caddy, and Authelia, as described in the &lt;a href="https://dominikbritz.com/posts/2024-01-22-laptop-home-server/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;first article of the series&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://dominikbritz.com/posts/immich-self-hosted-photos-with-cloud-backup/featured.jpg"/></item><item><title>Streamlined Nextcloud With OpenID Connect Authentication</title><link>https://dominikbritz.com/posts/streamlined-nextcloud-with-openid-connect-authentication/</link><pubDate>Mon, 05 Feb 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dominikbritz.com/posts/streamlined-nextcloud-with-openid-connect-authentication/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This article explains how to set up a fast and efficient Nextcloud as file management tool with OpenID Connect to Authelia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is part of my series on creating a home server on an old laptop. I&amp;rsquo;m assuming that you&amp;rsquo;ve set up Docker, Caddy, and Authelia, as described in the &lt;a href="https://dominikbritz.com/posts/2024-01-22-laptop-home-server/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;first article of the series&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://dominikbritz.com/posts/streamlined-nextcloud-with-openid-connect-authentication/featured.jpg"/></item><item><title>Laptop Home Server Build</title><link>https://dominikbritz.com/posts/2024-01-22-laptop-home-server/</link><pubDate>Tue, 23 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dominikbritz.com/posts/2024-01-22-laptop-home-server/</guid><description>&lt;div
 
